# `prev of` a name that exists ONLY as a function's local — both sides must DIE.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is a leak the runtime cannot see. Part 2a routes a
# temporal function's locals through the GLOBAL env and no env-removal API
# exists, so after the function returns its local is still resolvable there —
# indistinguishable from a real module binding. The VM raises "undefined
# variable 't'" (the tape holds history under the name, but the READ requires
# the binding in scope); the first AOT answered "one" from the tape, rc 0.
#
# The fix is compile-time: a module-scope `prev` of a name never bound at
# module scope emits the VM's exact raise. Residual corner, accepted and
# stated in the emitter: one temporal function interrogating ANOTHER's leaked
# local still diverges — unfixable without an env-removal API upstream.

define g(k) as:
    local t is "one"
    t is "two"
    return 0

print of (g of 1)
print of (prev of t)
print of "unreachable"
